# Normalise text files to LF in the repository.
#
# src/App.jsx was stored with CRLF while the working copy sat under
# core.autocrlf=true. Any tool that rewrote the file with LF endings then
# produced a diff touching all ~50,000 lines, burying a 24-line change and
# making review impossible. Declaring the convention here means git converts
# on commit regardless of which editor or script wrote the file, so the diff
# always reflects the actual change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
